Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["InfraEchoFunction", "ObjectName",
 CellID->1224892054,ExpressionUUID->"8393d601-4014-44ba-afc9-60862df940ec"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell["   ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->"2a57bb28-ea60-4cf6-acb3-da5018028832"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["InfraEchoFunction"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraCausality/ref/InfraEchoFunction", 
     "WolframInstitute/InfraCausality Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["a", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["b", "TI"]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "299fc0f2-9a32-4843-951f-d99e5253195a"],
 "\[LineSeparator]",
 "is the echo relation of the observer ",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 " via the observer ",
 StyleBox["b", "TI"],
 ": each tick of ",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 " goes to the ticks of ",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 " that receive the light returned from ",
 StyleBox["b", "TI"],
 ". Its members are the echo functions, the compositions of a message \
function from ",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 " to ",
 StyleBox["b", "TI"],
 " with a message function from ",
 StyleBox["b", "TI"],
 " back to ",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 ".",
 "\n"
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"0e8018f7-2010-46c7-ac46-b9e66f777fe4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Definition: with the message relations ",
 StyleBox["M", "TI"],
 "ab from ",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 " to ",
 StyleBox["b", "TI"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["M", "TI"],
 "ba from ",
 StyleBox["b", "TI"],
 " to ",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 " of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraMessageFunction"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraCausality/ref/InfraMessageFunction", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraCausality Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "7c6ec3cd-4d0f-4775-9b2d-8b1d5c184585"],
 ", the echo relation sends a tick ",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 " of ",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 " to Echo(",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 ") = \[Union] ",
 StyleBox["M", "TI"],
 "ba(",
 StyleBox["w", "TI"],
 ") over ",
 StyleBox["w", "TI"],
 " \[Element] ",
 StyleBox["M", "TI"],
 "ab(",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 "), the ticks of ",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 " lit by the return signals. An echo function is a composition ",
 StyleBox["t", "TI"],
 " \[SmallCircle] ",
 StyleBox["s", "TI"],
 " of a message function ",
 StyleBox["s", "TI"],
 " from ",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 " to ",
 StyleBox["b", "TI"],
 " and a message function ",
 StyleBox["t", "TI"],
 " from ",
 StyleBox["b", "TI"],
 " to ",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 ", both order-preserving selections (EPS axiom D1), defined on the ticks ",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 " of ",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 " whose signal returns, that is ",
 StyleBox["s", "TI"],
 "(",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 ") has a message back. Two pairs (",
 StyleBox["s", "TI"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["t", "TI"],
 ") can give the same echo function, and the members are the distinct \
composites."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"cc550c93-ef00-4428-92e5-3bc007ca71b1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Every echo function preserves the order of ",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 ", but not every order-preserving map into the echo relation is an echo \
function: a map with admissible images may factor only through a selection \
that reverses the order of two message images. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraEchoFunctionQ"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraCausality/ref/InfraEchoFunctionQ", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraCausality Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "c1d52b38-c3c2-4ff4-81cf-13ffc6249d4b"],
 " decides membership exactly and without enumeration: the map must be \
order-preserving with its domain among the ticks that have a message, and the \
layered selection DAG of ",
 StyleBox["M", "TI"],
 "ab, restricted to the images ",
 StyleBox["w", "TI"],
 " of a tick ",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 " with ",
 StyleBox["f", "TI"],
 "(",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 ") \[Element] ",
 StyleBox["M", "TI"],
 "ba(",
 StyleBox["w", "TI"],
 ") (or with ",
 StyleBox["M", "TI"],
 "ba(",
 StyleBox["w", "TI"],
 ") empty when ",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 " is outside the domain of ",
 StyleBox["f", "TI"],
 "), with an edge between equal images of consecutive ticks kept only when ",
 StyleBox["f", "TI"],
 " takes the same value on both, must have a path from the first tick to the \
last. A path is a selection ",
 StyleBox["s", "TI"],
 ", and ",
 StyleBox["t", "TI"],
 " is read off it as ",
 StyleBox["t", "TI"],
 "(",
 StyleBox["s", "TI"],
 "(",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 ")) = ",
 StyleBox["f", "TI"],
 "(",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 "); ",
 StyleBox["t", "TI"],
 " is order-preserving because ",
 StyleBox["f", "TI"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["s", "TI"],
 " are, and it extends to the ticks of ",
 StyleBox["b", "TI"],
 " that ",
 StyleBox["s", "TI"],
 " misses because each message image is an initial segment of the future of \
its tick on ",
 StyleBox["b", "TI"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"a444a246-c0d4-4008-82b5-44310ac15ad3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The echo is the round trip of radar: the observer ",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 " sends a signal at tick ",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 ", it is reflected at ",
 StyleBox["b", "TI"],
 ", and it comes back at a later tick. In Minkowski space the echo is a \
single event, and the emission and reception times give the radar time and \
distance of the reflection event. On a graph the echo of a tick can be \
several ticks, or none when the signal misses ",
 StyleBox["b", "TI"],
 " or the return misses ",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 "; every echo lies strictly after its tick."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"4790001d-5af5-4e93-8ca8-49ad41007d15"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The head holds its two observers and computes nothing. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraMeasurement"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraMeasurement", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "595f9ec4-b7d3-48ba-910b-97b08ba240d7"],
 " reads it on a graph:"
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"a17e8f8e-d33b-4b02-95ce-a885d6692104"],

Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "7f2c4f0d-7375-4e35-8d60-6f3fa2199e88"], Cell["Property", "TableText",
     FontWeight->Bold,ExpressionUUID->"01baa63f-7f62-451a-b498-202583783cbb"],
     Cell["Value", "TableText",
     FontWeight->Bold,ExpressionUUID->"af225998-a531-4e51-bf89-741f6d6f3611"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "6e3f3828-4d12-4fe7-93a0-cddc5ea39be8"], Cell[TextData[Cell[
    BoxData["\"\<Relation\>\""], "InlineFormula",
     FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
     "06c865f9-7839-40b7-91fa-04abe5b34bb6"]], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "3da08612-0d46-4c40-a8ae-e02f0ec33ea2"], Cell[TextData[{
     "the association ",
     StyleBox["v", "TI"],
     " \[RightArrow] Echo(",
     StyleBox["v", "TI"],
     ") over every tick of ",
     StyleBox["a", "TI"],
     ", echoes in the order of ",
     StyleBox["a", "TI"]
    }], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"828c1d52-a0da-4c76-9809-2b128cfa1d3a"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "36450091-69e5-4740-8d88-e39344b3b2a2"], Cell[TextData[Cell[
    BoxData["\"\<Graph\>\""], "InlineFormula",
     FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
     "a0a016a2-3cdc-49e1-bec4-d9e6b1a93be4"]], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "6f74cb0e-42e2-44b5-8dd4-6d5f7d8318bc"], Cell[TextData[{
     "the directed graph ",
     StyleBox["v", "TI"],
     " \[RightArrow] ",
     StyleBox["u", "TI"],
     " of the relation, on the ticks of ",
     StyleBox["a", "TI"]
    }], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"2441d1b9-3922-4fcb-b8b0-f1c99b809363"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "a3f43ff4-5b55-4838-a65e-e3d99232c106"], Cell[TextData[Cell[
    BoxData["\"\<Cardinality\>\""], "InlineFormula",
     FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
     "8ccfe8ee-f1e3-41aa-9449-c779e536ce33"]], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "7970cdaf-eec5-4e13-a800-6e20ce65a0a1"], Cell["\<\
the number of distinct echo functions, by enumeration of the two sets of \
message functions; at most the product of the two message cardinalities\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"91533e51-6983-478b-a63b-efe5ffd3801c"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "71fb36be-4fe3-4551-b4d3-f80d6883f2f5"], Cell[TextData[Cell[
    BoxData["\"\<Faithful\>\""], "InlineFormula",
     FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
     "36f123e2-aba9-4f32-b252-35427944e80b"]], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "0dbe513f-afc8-4216-b270-09717bb60f07"], Cell[TextData[Cell[BoxData[
    "True"], "InlineFormula",
     FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
     "da42bf89-04b6-4acf-8508-303bac74ffe1"]], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "5c9c767c-3652-4a39-b32b-956b510d67aa"]}
  }]], "2ColumnTableMod",ExpressionUUID->"02d27044-38df-4d23-97f5-\
ff9ab144d61d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A member is an association from ticks of ",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 " to ticks of ",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 ". ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraEchoFunctionQ"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraCausality/ref/InfraEchoFunctionQ", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraCausality Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "7c3e5478-6b48-4f01-a8af-a5195e21add2"],
 " decides membership, and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraMemberQ"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraMemberQ", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "3fbf4feb-6dc6-4a1d-be56-c42b0096dea4"],
 " is the same test; ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["RandomInfraEchoFunction"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraCausality/ref/RandomInfraEchoFunction", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraCausality Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "2e70d407-bc53-4246-a57e-62bba871eb33"],
 " draws members or enumerates them. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraSubstrateHighlight"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraSubstrateHighlight", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "daaa0ea6-2bdd-4dda-aa30-dfc7e2ae9b0d"],
 " draws the head as the outgoing and returning light rays."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"ff2f4db1-7ffc-4f57-9b61-71071b764023"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The EPS defects of the echo relation are the four defects of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraMessageFunction"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraCausality/ref/InfraMessageFunction", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraCausality Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "41fae07d-719e-4a52-92e2-444725e589b9"],
 " read on the relation ",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 " \[RightArrow] Echo(",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 "), on the window of ",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 " left by the option ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\"\<Margin\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "b"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4bff3e0a-0ec2-4db1-a655-1a5e847aa058"],
 " (a fourth argument, default 0), with the echoes anywhere on ",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 ": ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<DomainDefect\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d484bc08-1aee-469d-892d-5754a8526508"],
 " the fraction of window ticks without an echo, ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<FunctionDefect\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a821276e-605f-40f7-8dac-e56e5c6a44d3"],
 " the mean of max(0, ",
 "|",
 "Echo(",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 ")",
 "|",
 " \[Minus] 1) / max(1, ",
 "|",
 "Echo(",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 ")",
 "|",
 "), ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<InjectivityDefect\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d2d90d0c-e822-4413-8dcb-7ca7d3dd2326"],
 " 1 \[Minus] \[Nu] / ",
 StyleBox["n", "TI"],
 " with \[Nu] a maximum matching of the relation, and ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<OrderDefect\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c19c704f-7751-47b2-98bf-6d3baf08824d"],
 " the fraction of ordered window pairs ",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 " before ",
 StyleBox["w", "TI"],
 " with an echo of ",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 " after an echo of ",
 StyleBox["w", "TI"],
 ", a tie of single echoes counting against injectivity and not against \
order. In Minkowski space the echo of an inertial observer via another is a \
monotone injection of its clock into itself, and all four vanish; on a graph \
they vanish together exactly when every window tick has one echo and the \
echoes strictly increase along ",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 ", which is what ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["EPSMessageAxiomQ"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraCausality/ref/EPSMessageAxiomQ", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraCausality Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "f7d29793-1830-4ea2-9f82-6e44ce5d7975"],
 " of the echo head tests."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"c9ad7c90-1138-4495-b5be-cb6a3b379b36"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<KFactor\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "94fca49a-1ee1-491f-850d-51acddd392a8"],
 " is the square root of the ratio of echo to tick spans of the earliest-echo \
selection: with ",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["w", "TI"],
 " the first and last window ticks that have an echo, \[Sqrt]((pos ",
 StyleBox["e", "TI"],
 "(",
 StyleBox["w", "TI"],
 ") \[Minus] pos ",
 StyleBox["e", "TI"],
 "(",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 ")) / (pos ",
 StyleBox["w", "TI"],
 " \[Minus] pos ",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 ")), positions counted on ",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 ". In Minkowski space an observer receding at speed ",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 " returns the radar signal of another after ",
 StyleBox["k", "TI"],
 "\.b2 times the sending time, with ",
 StyleBox["k", "TI"],
 " = \[Sqrt]((1 + ",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 ")/(1 \[Minus] ",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 ")) the Bondi factor, so the square root is the Bondi factor under \
reciprocity, ",
 StyleBox["k", "TI"],
 "ab = ",
 StyleBox["k", "TI"],
 "ba. The reading uses the clock of ",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 " alone: on the diamond lattice the resting chain {(",
 StyleBox["m", "TI"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["m", "TI"],
 ")} echoed by the chain {((",
 StyleBox["p", "TI"],
 " + 1)",
 StyleBox["m", "TI"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["pm", "TI"],
 ")} of velocity 1/(2",
 StyleBox["p", "TI"],
 " + 1) reads exactly \[Sqrt]((",
 StyleBox["p", "TI"],
 " + 1)/",
 StyleBox["p", "TI"],
 "), the Bondi factor, although the moving chain's ticks are not its proper \
time. On sprinklings the longest chains between two events wander, so two \
observers with a given endpoint velocity share stretches of their worldlines \
and the reading scatters widely at a few hundred events."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"30f87444-0560-4962-990f-57cd14af5822"],

Cell["Corresponding notions:", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"a27b1071-9436-4070-9fae-a3b7c48d3eb1"],

